        "candidate": "GraphTheory.connectivity.matching",
        "note": "Upstream matching M := {subset M <= E(G)} /\\ {in M &, forall e1 e2 x, x \\in e1 -> x \\in e2 -> e1 = e2} is the corpus notion for X14, X15 and X180 (X180's fg_edges G equals E(G): Extremal.migration.matching.fg_edgesE). The API and grounding (empty set, single edge, K_2, K_3, adjacent edges rejected, closure under subsets, members are 2-sets) are in Packing.foundations.matching; the presentation lemmas should move to GTBase.common when the misc/extremal certificates are simplified (second-area rule). The hypergraph and whole-graph representations stay split.",
